Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 18:36:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 558/572] refactor(st): drop unused A/B bootfs/rootfs IO
 policies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"feat(st): search FIP entry explicitly in plat_fwu_set_images_source"
made plat_fwu_set_images_source() look up only the FIP entry in the
FWU metadata instead of iterating every entry. The per-image IO
policies, image IDs and partition GUIDs previously added for the
bootfs/rootfs A/B images are therefore unused: BL2 never opens or
authenticates them, only U-Boot/Linux do.

Revert the now dead code:
 - "feat(st): enable A/B redundancy support" (FWU_BOOTFS_ID/
   FWU_ROOTFS_ID IO policies, block specs, image auth IDs)
 - "feat(st): add extended bootloader GUID" (XBOOTLDR_GUID)
 - "feat(st): add Linux data partition GUID"
   (LINUX_FILE_SYSTEM_DATA_GUID)

The STM32_EXTRA_PARTS adjustment from the first revert is still
needed on both STM32MP1 and STM32MP2 though: load_partition_table()
parses the GPT sequentially into a fixed-size list.list[]
(PLAT_PARTITION_MAX_ENTRIES = STM32_TF_A_COPIES + STM32_EXTRA_PARTS)
and silently truncates entries beyond that size. Since a partition's
position in the GPT is not guaranteed, PLAT_PARTITION_MAX_ENTRIES
must cover the whole table -- including the bootfs-a/b, rootfs-a/b,
vendorfs and u-boot-env partitions added by
STM32MP_PSA_FWU_AB_SUPPORT=1 -- or the FIP/metadata partitions could
be dropped from the parsed list if located after that cutoff. Restore
that +6 adjustment on both platforms.

